1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,860
Ah Caroline... come on in. Sit down.

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:04,000
Thanks.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
So how's the dissertation planning going?

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,800
Well Dr Schulmann, I'm still having a lot of trouble deciding on a title.

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:14,220
Well, that's perfectly normal at this stage

6
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,570
And this is what your tutorials will help you to do.

7
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:18,130
Right.

8
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:23,724
What we'll do is jot down some points that might help you in your decision.

9
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:28,200
First of all, you have chosen your general topic area, haven't you?

10
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,600
Yes, it's the fishing industry.

11
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:34,200
Oh yes, that was one of the areas you mentioned

12
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:38,250
Now, what aspects of the course are you good at?

13
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:44,750
Well, I think I'm coping well with statistics, and I'm never bored by it.

14
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:46,630
Good, Anything else?

15
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:49,632
Well, I found computer modelling fascinating -

16
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:54,980
I have no problem following what's being taught

17
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:58,640
whereas quite a few of my classmates find it difficult.

18
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:04,680
Well, that's very good. Do you think these might be areas you could bring into your dissertation?

19
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:10,705
Oh yes, if possible. It's just that I'm having difficulty thinking how I can do that.

20
00:01:10,705 --> 00:01:14,470
You see I feel I don't have sufficient background information.

21
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:17,870
I see. Well, do you take notes?

22
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:23,370
I'm very weak at note-taking. My teachers always used to say that.

23
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:28,700
Well, I think you really need to work on these weaknesses before you go any further.

24
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:29,970
What do you suggest?

25
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:34,440
Well, I can go through the possible strategies with you

26
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,430
and let you decide where to go from there.

27
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:37,610
Okay, thanks.

28
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:41,584
Well, some people find it helpful to organise peer-group discussions -

29
00:01:41,584 --> 00:01:47,040
you know, each week a different person studies a different topic

30
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,340
and shares it with the group.

31
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:50,220
Oh right.

32
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:55,170
It really helps build confidence, you know, having to present something to others.

33
00:01:55,170 --> 00:01:56,310
I can see that.

34
00:01:56,310 --> 00:02:00,300
The drawback is that everyone in the group seems to share the same ideas

35
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,850
they keep being repeated in all the dissertations.

36
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:04,830
Okay.

37
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:08,267
You could also try a service called 'Student Support'.

38
00:02:08,267 --> 00:02:14,760
It's designed to give you a structured programme over a number of weeks to develop your skills.

39
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,900
Sounds good.

40
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:21,300
Yes, unfortunately there are only a few places. But it's worth looking into.

41
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:25,600
Yes, of course. I know I've got to work on my study skills.

42
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:29,640
And then there are several study skills books you can consult.

43
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:30,320
Right.

44
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:32,860
They'll be a good source of reference

45
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:36,880
but the problem is they are sometimes too general.

46
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:38,720
Yes, that's what I've found.

47
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:46,570
Other than that I would strongly advise quite simple ideas like using a card index.

48
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:49,380
Well, yes, I've never done that before.

49
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:51,880
It's simple, but it really works

50
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:56,690
because you have to get points down in a small space.

51
00:02:56,690 --> 00:03:02,638
Another thing I always advise is don't just take your notes and forget about them.

52
00:03:02,638 --> 00:03:07,000
Read everything three times - that'll really fix them in your mind.

53
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,740
Yes, I can see it'd take discipline but...

54
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:16,040
Well, if you establish good study skills at this stage they'll be with you all your life.

55
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,770
Oh yes, I completely agree.

56
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:21,800
It's just that I don't seem to be able to discipline myself

57
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:24,000
I need to talk things over.

58
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:30,840
Well, we'll be continuing these tutorials of course. Let's arrange next month's now.

59
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:39,900
Let's see, I can see you virtually any time during the week starting 22nd January.

60
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:46,650
What about the 24th? I'm free in the afternoon.

61
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:50,730
Sorry, I'm booked then. What about the following day?

62
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:53,800
Thursday? I can make the morning.

63
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,360
Fine, we'll go for the 25th then.

64
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,870
That's great, thanks.
